 (30 -1)(70 -1) but that might complicate. Alternatively, 29*70 would be 2030, then subtract 29 gives 2030 -29 = 2001. Yep, same result. So that seems correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 29 and 69 is 2001.\n</think>\n\n",
