t one position to the left): 600\nAdd them together: 135 + 600 = 735. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using distributive property: 15*(50 - 1) = 15*50 - 15*1 = 750 - 15 = 735. Oh, that works too. So that confirms it again. \n\nI think that's correct. Let me check with a calculator in my head. 15 times 50 would be 750, so subtracting 15 gives 735. Yep, that's consistent. So I feel confident the answer is 735.\n"]
