ne position to the left, so 801 shifted becomes 8010)\nAdding 534 +8010 gives 8544. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (90 -1)(90 +6)? Wait, no, that might complicate. Alternatively, maybe (90 -1)*96? Hmm, not sure. Alternatively, 89*96 = (90 -1)*96 = 90*96 - 96. Let me see if that gives the same result. 90*96 is 8640, minus 96 would be 8640 -96 = 8544. Yep, same answer. So that checks out.\n\nSo the steps are correct. Therefore, the product of 89 and 96 is indeed 8544. I think that's solid. Let me just recap the steps as per the template:\n\n1. Multiply 89 by 6 (the ones place of 96): 534\n2. Multiply 89 by 90 (the tens place, which is 9*10): 8010\n3. Add them together: 534 + 8010 = 8544\n\nYep, that's exactly what I did. So I think that's the right answer. No mistakes in the calculations detected. All cross-verification methods lead to the same result. Confident with that.\n</think>\n\n",
