760, then plus 88 is 5848. Wait, is that right? Wait, 5160 + 688: 5160 + 600 is 5760, then +88 gives 5848. Hmm, but let me check again. Alternatively, 5160 + 688: 5000 + 160 + 600 + 88 = 5000 + (160+600)=5000+760=5760 +88=5848. Yes, that's correct.\n\nWait, but let me confirm the multiplication another way to be sure. Maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n   86\n\u00d7 68\n-------\nFirst multiply 86 by 8: 688\nThen multiply 86 by 60 (so shift one position to the left):\n   86\n\u00d7 60\n-----\n5160\nThen add them: 688 +5160=5848. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, cross-multiplying: (80+6)(60+8) = 80\u00d760 + 80\u00d78 +6\u00d760 +6\u00d78 = 4800 + 640 + 360 +48 = 4800+640=5440; 5440+360=5800; 5800+48=5848. Yep, same answer. So the steps are correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 5848. Let me just make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors here.\n\nWait, another check: 86 \u00d7 70 would be 6020, but since it's 68, which is 70-2, so 6020 - (86\u00d72)=6020-172=5848. That's another way to compute. Yep, that works too. So all methods converge to 5848. So I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n",
