matches the previous result. So that's reassuring.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method like the lattice method or some other trick, but since I already have two methods giving me 3731, I feel more confident. Let me just do the standard multiplication again step by step to be thorough.\n\nMultiplying 91 by 41:\n\nFirst, write it down as:\n\n\u2003\u200391  \n\u00d7\u00a041  \n------  \n\u2003\u2003? (91 \u00d7 1)  \n+ ??? (91 \u00d7 40, shifted one position to the left)  \n------------  \nTotal\n\nSo, first step: 91 \u00d7 1 = 91. Write that down.\n\nSecond step: 91 \u00d7 4. Since it's the tens place, this is actually 91 \u00d7 40. So multiply 91 by 4:\n\n91 \u00d7 4: 90\u00d74=360, 1\u00d74=4 \u2192 364. Then, since it's the tens place, we add a zero at the end, making it 3640. So writing that shifted one position to the left:\n\n\u2003\u00a03640  \n+\u2003\u00a091  \n-------  \nNow adding those two:\n\n3640  \n+\u00a091  \n------  \nStart from the right: 0 +1 =1, 4 +9=13 (write 3, carryover 1), 6 + 0 +1 (carryover) =7, then 3 remains. Wait, no:\n\nWait, actually, adding 3640 and 91:\n\n3640  \n+\u00a0 91  \n= ?\n\nLet's line them up properly:\n\n\u20033640  \n+\u2003\u00a091  \n=3640 + 91. \n\nAdding units place: 0 +1 =1  \nTens place: 4 +9 =13. Write down 3, carryover 1.  \nHundreds place: 6 + 0 +1 (carryover) =7  \nThousands place: 3 remains.  \nSo total is 3731. Yep, same result. \n\nSo, all methods are pointing to 3731. Therefore, the product of 91 and 41 is 3731. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. Just to be extra sure, maybe do a quick check using estimation. 90 times 40 is 3600, and 91 is a bit more, 41 is a bit more, so 3600 plus some. 3731 is reasonable. Alternatively, 91*40 would be 3640, plus another 91 gives 3731. Yep, that's correct.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 91 and 41?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 41 has two digits, so we can break the multiplication into two steps.\n1. Multiply 91 by the ones place digit (1) of 41:  \n   \\(91 \\times 1 = 91\\).\n2. Multiply 91 by the tens place digit (40) of 41:  \n   \\(91 \\times 40 = 3,\\!640\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(91 + 3,\\!640 = 3,\\!731\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{3731}.",
