 720 + 7200 = 7920. That should be the correct answer. I think that's all. Let me just make sure there's no step missing. Since 99 is two digits, only two steps needed. Yep, looks good.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 80 and 99?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 99 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps.\n1. Multiply 80 by the ones place digit 9 of 99:  \n   \\(80 \\times 9 = 720\\).\n2. Multiply 80 by the tens place digit 90 of 99:  \n   \\(80 \\times 90 = 7200\\).  \n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(720 + 7200 = 7920\\).  \n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{7920}.",
