ting 90×75: 90×70=6300 and 90×5=450, so total 6300+450=6750. Then subtract 75: 6750 -75 = 6675. \n\nHmm, that also gives the same answer. Good, so three different methods all leading to 6675. That gives me more confidence that the answer is correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use some other arithmetic tricks. For instance, 75 is 3/4 of 100, so 89 ×75 = 89 × (3/4 ×100) = (89 ×3/4) ×100. Let me compute 89 ×3 first: that's 267, then divided by 4 gives 66.75, then multiplied by 100 is 6675. That also works. \n\nWait, that's interesting. So 89 times 3/4 is 66.75, and times 100 gives 6675. That method also confirms it. \n\nAnother way could be using the fact that 75 is 25×3, so 89×25×3. Let me see: 89×25. Since 25×4=100, so 89×25 is (89×4)×25/4 = 356 × (25/4) but that might complicate. Alternatively, 25×89: 25×90 would be 2250, minus 25 gives 2250-25=2225. Then multiply by 3: 2225×3=6675. Yep, that works too. \n\nSo all these different methods are leading me to the same answer, so I think 6675 is correct. I don't see any mistakes in my calculations, so I'm confident that's the right product.\n"] 14%|█▍        | 71/500 [39:33<4:03:35, 34.07s/it]
