n multiply by 80 (so shifted one position to the left):\n73 x80 = 5840\n\nAdding those together: 365 + 5840 = 6205. That's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method like the distributive property. (70 +3)(80 +5) = 70*80 + 70*5 + 3*80 + 3*5. Let's see:\n\n70*80 = 5600\n\n70*5 = 350\n\n3*80 = 240\n\n3*5 =15\n\nAdding all those together: 5600 + 350 is 5950, plus 240 is 6190, plus 15 is 6205. Yep, same result. So that's consistent. \n\nWait, but I want to make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors. Let me check each part again.\n\nFirst, 73 x5:\n\n70*5 = 350, 3*5=15. 350+15=365. Correct.\n\n73 x80:\n\n73*8 is 584, so times 10 is 5840. Correct.\n\nAdding 365 +5840: 365 +5840. Let me add 5840 + 300 = 6140, then +65 = 6205. Yes.\n\nAlternatively, 5840 + 365:\n\nStarting from the units digit: 0 +5 =5, 4 +6=10 (carryover 1), 8 +3 +1=12 (carryover 1), 5 +0 +1=6. So that gives 6205. Correct.\n\nOkay, so all methods confirm that the product is 6205. Therefore, the final answer should be 6205.\n</think>\n\n",
