   57  (57 x 1)\n    1710  (57 x 30, shifted one position to the left)\n    -----\n    1767\n\nYes, that's the same result. Another way could be to use the distributive property: 57*(30 +1) = 57*30 +57*1 = 1710 +57 =1767. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 57*31 as (50 +7)*(30 +1), but that might complicate more. Let's see:\n\n50*30 = 1500\n\n50*1 =50\n\n7*30=210\n\n7*1=7\n\nAdding all those together: 1500 +50 is 1550, plus 210 is 1760, plus 7 is 1767. Yep, same answer.\n\nOkay, so I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in the steps. The final product should be 1767.\n</think>\n\n",
