\n\u00d720  \n________  \nFirst, multiply 26 by 0:  \n26 \u00d7 0 = 0. Write down 0.  \n\nThen multiply 26 by 2 (the tens place, so actually 20).  \n26 \u00d7 2 = 52. Since it's the tens place, we write 52 but shifted one position to the left, making it 520.  \n\nNow add the two lines:  \n0  \n+520  \n=520  \n\nYes, that's correct. I don't see any errors here. So the product should be 520.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 26 and 20?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 20 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps:\n1. Multiply 26 by the ones place digit 0 of 20:  \n   \\(26 \\times 0 = 0\\).\n2. Multiply 26 by the tens place digit 2 (representing 20):  \n   \\(26 \\times 20 = 520\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(0 + 520 = 520\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{520}.",
