 Let's see, 55 times 63. Maybe breaking down 63 into 60 +3, which is exactly what I did. So (55*60)+(55*3) = 3300 +165 = 3465. Yep, that seems right. Alternatively, maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   55\nx 63\n-------\n  165  (55*3)\n+3300  (55*60, shifted one position to the left)\n-------\n  3465\n\nYep, that adds up. So I think that's the correct answer. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my head. 55*60 is 3300, and 55*3 is 165, so adding gives 3465. Definitely correct.\n"]
