 = 72\u00d7(60+3) = 72\u00d760 + 72\u00d73 = 4320 + 216 = 4536. \n\nAlright, that all checks out. I think that's the correct answer. Let me just make sure I didn't mix up any digits. The original numbers were 72 and 63, right? Yes. 72 times 60 is 4320, 72 times 3 is 216. Adding them gives 4536. I don't see any mistakes here. \n\nSo following the template, the reasoning should list each step, then sum them. The answer is 4536. Okay, I think that's it.\n</think>\n\n",
