3 is 184. Adding those: 230 + 184. 200 + 100 = 300, 30 + 84 = 114, so total 300 + 114 = 414. Same answer again. So that's good.\n\nHmm, maybe I can also do 18 \u00d7 23 as (20 - 2) \u00d7 23. Wait, that might complicate, but let's see: 20\u00d723 = 460, minus 2\u00d723 = 46. So 460 - 46 = 414. That works too. \n\nAll methods lead to 414, so I'm confident that's the correct product.\n</think>\n\n",
