. Let me compute 80*39. 80*40 would be 3200, subtract 80 gives 3120. Yep, that's correct. Okay, so all methods agree. So I think that's right. \n\nBut the question specifies the reasoning in a template where they split the number into ones, tens, etc. So since 39 is two digits, the reasoning steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 80 by the ones digit (9) to get 720.\n\n2. Multiply 80 by the tens digit (3) but since it's the tens place, it's actually 30, so 80*30 = 2400.\n\nThen add them together: 720 + 2400 = 3120.\n\nSo the answer is 3120. I think that's solid. Let me just ensure I didn't mix up any steps. The key here is breaking down 39 into 30 + 9, multiplying each part by 80, then summing. Yep, that's the standard method. Alright, confident with that.\n</think>\n\n",
