88*9 shifted one position: 7920\nAdding 264 + 7920 gives 8184. \n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property: (80 + 8)(90 + 3) = 80*90 + 80*3 + 8*90 + 8*3. \n\nCalculating each term:\n80*90 = 7200\n80*3 = 240\n8*90 = 720\n8*3 =24\n\nAdding all together: 7200 + 240 = 7440; 7440 + 720 = 8160; 8160 +24=8184. Yep, same result. \n\nI think that's correct. Let me just do a quick check using another method, maybe the difference of squares or something else. Wait, 88 and 93 are close to 90.5, but maybe not the best approach. Alternatively, 93 is 90 +3, so 88*(90+3) is exactly what we did. \n\nAlternatively, 88*93 = (90 -2)*93 = 90*93 - 2*93. Let me compute that. 90*93: 90*90=8100, 90*3=270, so total 8370. Then subtract 2*93=186. So 8370 - 186 = 8184. Yep, same answer. \n\nAlright, so all methods are confirming that the product is 8184. So I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n",
