0. I think that's the correct answer. Let me just do a quick check with another method. Maybe 22 times 90. Since multiplication is commutative, it should be the same. Let's see, 22\u00d790. 22\u00d79 is 198, then add a zero to get 1980. Yep, same answer. Okay, I feel confident that 1980 is the right product.\n</think>\n\n",
