her method. Let's do straight multiplication:\n\n19\ntimes 99. Let's write it out:\n\n   19\nx 99\n--------\nFirst, multiply 19 by 9 (units place): 171\nThen multiply 19 by 9 (tens place, so actually 90), so 19*9=171, then shifted one left gives 1710\nAdding those together: 171 +1710 = 1881. Yep, same result. Okay, confident that's right.\n"]
