y another method to verify. Let's do the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   92\nx29\n-----\nFirst multiply 92 by 9: 92*9=828 (as before)\nThen multiply 92 by 20 (since the 2 is in the tens place, so 2*10). So 92*20=1840. \nAdding those two: 828 + 1840 = 2668. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (90 + 2)*(20 +9) = 90*20 + 90*9 + 2*20 + 2*9 = 1800 + 810 +40 +18 = 1800+810 is 2610, plus 40 is 2650, plus 18 is 2668. Yep, same result. \n\nOkay, so I think the answer is 2668. Wait, but let me confirm with another approach. Let me do 92*30 which is 2760, then subtract 92 to get 2760-92=2668. That's the same as before. So I think that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 92 and 29 is 2668.\n"]
