ted by recognizing that 75 is 3/4 of 100, but that might complicate. Alternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (20 -1) * 75 = 20*75 - 1*75. \n\nCalculating 20*75: that's 1500. Then subtract 75: 1500 -75 = 1425. Yep, same result. So that confirms the previous answer. \n\nAlternatively, maybe breaking down 75 into 70 +5, which is the same as the original method. So both ways give 1425. That seems right. I think that's correct. So the steps are as per the template, two steps here because 75 has two digits. \n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 1425. I should present the reasoning as per the template, showing each step clearly.\n"] 35%|███▌      | 176/500 [1:36:08<2:29:22, 27.66s/it] 35%|███▌      | 177/500 [1:36:37<2:32:26, 28.32s/it]
