 is 16. Adding those: 1500 + 400 = 1900, 60 +16=76, so total 1976. \n\nOkay, so all methods give me the same result. So the product should be 1976. Wait, but let me check with a calculator in my head again. 52*40 would be 2080, right? Because 52*40 is 52*4*10=208*10=2080. But since it's 38, which is 2 less than 40, subtract 52*2=104 from 2080. 2080-104 is 1976. Yep, that works. So the answer is definitely 1976. I think that's solid. \n\nJust to recap the steps as per the template: since 38 is two digits, we split into two steps. Multiply 52 by 8 (ones place) to get 416, then multiply 52 by 30 (tens place) to get 1560. Adding those together gives 1976. That's exactly what I did. So the reasoning steps are correct. I don't see any mistakes here. All checks confirm the answer. Alright, confident with that.\n</think>\n\n",
