n +84 = 4704. That seems right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I should verify using another method to be sure. Let me try the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   48\nx 98\n-------\nFirst multiply 48 by 8: 384\nThen multiply 48 by 90 (shift one position to the left):\n48 x 90 = 4320\nAdd them: 384 + 4320 = 4704. \n\nSame answer. Alternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (50 - 2) * 48? Wait, no, the numbers are 48 and 98. Alternatively, 98 is 100 - 2. So 48*(100-2) = 48*100 - 48*2 = 4800 - 96 = 4704. Oh, that's another way and confirms the same result. \n\nSo the steps as per the template would be:\n\n1. Multiply 48 by 8 (the ones place) to get 384.\n\n2. Multiply 48 by 90 (the tens place) to get 4320.\n\nAdding those together gives 4704. So that should be the correct product.\n"]
