s it again. \n\nHmm, all methods are leading me to 6580. I think that's correct. Let me just do a rough estimate to check. 70 times 90 is 6300, and 70 times 4 is 280, so adding them gives around 6580. Since 70*94 is between 70*90 and 70*100, which are 6300 and 7000, so 6580 is in between. That makes sense. \n\nI don't see any errors here, so I think the product is indeed 6580.\n</think>\n\n",
