previous result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm. Let's write it out the traditional way:\n\n   42\nx 75\n-------\nFirst multiply 42 by 5: that's 210. Then multiply 42 by 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place, so 7*10). 42*70 is 2940. Then add 210 and 2940 to get 3150. Yep, same answer. \n\nI think that's correct. Let me confirm once more with another approach. Maybe breaking down 42 into 40 and 2. So (40+2)*75. That would be 40*75 + 2*75. 40*75 is 3000, since 40*75 is 40*70 + 40*5 = 2800 + 200 = 3000. Then 2*75 is 150. Adding 3000 + 150 gives 3150. Yep, same result. Okay, so all methods are giving me 3150, so I'm confident that's the right answer.\n"]
