 another method to be sure. Maybe the standard algorithm:\n\n   22\nx 33\n-------\nFirst multiply 22 by 3 (ones place): 66.\n\nThen multiply 22 by 30 (tens place): 660.\n\nAdding 66 + 660 gives 726. That's the same as before. \n\nAlternatively, I can do 22*33 = (20 + 2)*(30 +3). Let's expand that:\n\n20*30 = 600,\n\n20*3 = 60,\n\n2*30 = 60,\n\n2*3 = 6.\n\nAdding all those: 600 + 60 + 60 +6 = 600+120+6=726. Yep, same answer. So the product is indeed 726. Okay, so I think that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
