d follow as per the template, breaking down 49 into 40 and 9, multiplying each by 36, then adding. The answer is 1764.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 36 and 49?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 49 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens places.  \n1. Multiply 36 by the ones place digit (9):  \n   \\( 36 \\times 9 = 324 \\).  \n2. Multiply 36 by the tens place digit (40):  \n   \\( 36 \\times 40 = 1,\\!440 \\).  \nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 324 + 1,\\!440 = 1,\\!764 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **1,764**.",
