ait, I thought 49*23 should be... Let me verify with another method to be sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   49\nx23\n-------\nFirst multiply 49 by 3: 147\nThen multiply 49 by 20 (which is 980)\nAdd them: 147 + 980 = 1127. Yeah, that's the same.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (50 -1)*(20 +3) = 50*20 +50*3 -1*20 -1*3 = 1000 +150 -20 -3 = 1000+150 is 1150, minus 23 is 1127. Yep, same result. So the answer should be 1127. Okay, so the steps are correct. The reasoning in the template should follow those steps.\n"]
