es the other method. So that's probably correct. But let me try another way just to be thorough. Maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\nMultiply 91 by 98:\n\n       91\n     x 98\n     -----\nFirst multiply 91 by 8: 728 (as before)\nThen multiply 91 by 90 (since the 9 is in the tens place, so shifted one position to the left):\n       91\n     x 90\n     -----\n      8190\n\nAdding 728 and 8190 gives 8918. Yep, so all methods are pointing to 8918. I think that's the correct answer. Let me just confirm with a calculator-style multiplication:\n\n91 * 98. Let's see, 90*90 is 8100, 90*8 is 720, 1*90 is 90, and 1*8 is 8. Wait, no, that's breaking it into (90+1)(90+8). Wait, actually expanding (a+b)(c+d) = ac + ad + bc + bd. So 90*90 + 90*8 + 1*90 + 1*8 = 8100 + 720 +90 +8. Adding those: 8100 +720 is 8820, plus 90 is 8910, plus 8 is 8918. Yep, same result again. Okay, definitely confident now. The answer should be 8918.\n</think>\n\n",
