ng by the tens digit (9) as 9×10, so 13 × 9 ×10 = 117 ×10 = 1170. \n\nSo the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 13 by 0 (ones place) → 0.\n\n2. Multiply 13 by 9 (tens digit) → 117, then multiply by 10 to account for the tens place → 1170.\n\nThen adding those gives 0 + 1170 = 1170.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 1170.\n\nI think that's the correct approach. Let me check with another method to confirm. \n\nAlternatively, 13 × 90 can be thought of as 13 × 9 × 10. 13×9 is 117, then times 10 is 1170. That matches. \n\nAnother way: 10×90 = 900, 3×90 = 270; 900 + 270 = 1170. Yep, same result. \n\nSo the reasoning steps as per the template should be written as:\n\n1. Multiply 13 by the ones place digit 0 of 90 → 0.\n\n2. Multiply 13 by the tens place digit 90 (which is 9×10) → 13×9=117, then shifted left by one digit → 1170.\n\nSumming gives 0 + 1170 = 1170. So the final answer is 1170.\n"] 46%|████▋     | 232/500 [2:08:57<3:07:15, 41.92s/it] 47%|████▋     | 233/500 [2:09:15<2:35:03, 34.84s/it]
