00 + 120 +8 = 928. Wait, but 288 + 640. Let me do it vertically:\n\n  288\n+640\n-----\n  928\n\nYes, that's correct. So adding those two gives 928. Therefore, the product of 32 and 29 should be 928.\n\nWait, but let me double-check because sometimes when doing mental math, I might have made an error. Let me try another method. Maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n       32\n     x29\n     -----\n       288  (32 x 9)\n      640   (32 x 20, shifted one position to the left)\n     -----\n      928\n\nYes, that matches. Alternatively, maybe I can check using another method like the distributive property or adding. For instance, 32 times 30 would be 960, right? Because 32*30=960. But since it's 29, that's one less. So 960 - 32 = 928. That works. So that confirms it. So the answer is 928.\n</think>\n\n",
