hen multiply 37 by 80 (the tens place): 37*80=2960. Then add them: 333 +2960 = 3293. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property another way. Let's see, (30 +7)*(80 +9). Expanding that would be 30*80 + 30*9 +7*80 +7*9. Let's compute each term:\n\n30*80 = 2400\n\n30*9 = 270\n\n7*80 = 560\n\n7*9 = 63\n\nAdding them all: 2400 +270 = 2670; 2670 +560 = 3230; 3230 +63 = 3293. Same answer. Okay, so that checks out.\n\nHmm, another way: maybe using the fact that 89 is 90 -1. So 37*(90-1) = 37*90 -37*1. 37*90 is 37*9*10 = 333*10 = 3330. Then subtract 37 gives 3330 -37 = 3293. Yep, that works too. All methods lead to the same answer, so I must be correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 37 and 89 is 3293.\n"]
