ait a second, let me make sure I didn't make a mistake in the multiplication steps. Let me recalculate 59*3 again. 59 times 3: 50*3=150, 9*3=27, so 150+27=177. That's correct. Then 59*50: 59*5=295, so 295*10=2950. Correct. Adding 177 + 2950. Yes, that gives 3127. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method to cross-verify. Let's try the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   59\nx 53\n-------\nFirst multiply 59 by 3 (the ones place): 177\nThen multiply 59 by 50 (the tens place shifted one position to the left): 2950\nAdding them gives 177 + 2950 = 3127. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (60 -1)(50 +3) = 60*50 + 60*3 -1*50 -1*3 = 3000 + 180 -50 -3 = 3000 +180 is 3180, minus 50 is 3130, minus 3 is 3127. Yep, same result. So that's good. \n\nSo the final answer should be 3127. Let me just check with a calculator in my mind. 59*50 is 2950, plus 59*3 is 177, total 3127. Yep, that seems right. I think that's the correct product.\n"] 57%|█████▋    | 286/500 [2:37:15<2:10:40, 36.64s/it] 57%|█████▋    | 287/500 [2:37:42<1:59:10, 33.57s/it]
