hat gives 246, but since it's the tens place, shift one position left, so 2460.\n\nAdd 41 +2460: 2460 +41 =2501. \n\nAlright, so all methods are leading me to 2501. Therefore, I think that's the correct answer. But just to be 100% sure, let me do it another way. Let's compute 41×60 first, which is 2460, then add 41 to get 2501. Yes. Alternatively, 61×40 = 2440, plus 61×1 =61, so 2440+61=2501. That's another way. Yep, that works too. \n\nSo after verifying multiple times, I'm confident the product of 41 and 61 is 2501.\n"]
