830, then add the remaining 17: 2830 +17 = 2847. So the total is 2847. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can check using another method, like the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   39\nx 73\n-------\nFirst multiply 39 by 3: 117\nThen multiply 39 by 70 (which is 2730, as before)\nAdd them: 117 + 2730 = 2847. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property: (40 -1)(70 +3) = 40*70 +40*3 -1*70 -1*3 = 2800 +120 -70 -3 = 2800+120 is 2920, minus 70 is 2850, minus 3 is 2847. That matches too. So I think that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the product of 39 and 73 is 2847.\n</think>\n\n",
