t out:\n\n   16\nx 95\n-------\nFirst multiply 16 by 5: 80. Then multiply 16 by 90 (so shift one position to the left):\n\n16 x 90 = 1440. Then add 80 + 1440 = 1520. That seems right. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like the distributive property: (10 + 6) * 95? Wait, no, maybe breaking down 95 into 100 -5. Let me try that. \n\n16 * 95 = 16*(100 -5) = 16*100 - 16*5 = 1600 - 80 = 1520. Oh, that's another way and it gives the same result. So that confirms it. \n\nSo all the methods point to 1520. Therefore, the final answer should be 1520. Let me just make sure I didn't mix up any numbers in my steps. The first step with 5 gives 80, the second with 90 gives 1440, adding them gives 1520. Yes, that's correct. I think that's solid.\n</think>\n\n",
