em together: 153 + 3570 = 3723. Yep, that matches. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (50 + 1)(70 + 3) = 50*70 + 50*3 + 1*70 + 1*3 = 3500 + 150 + 70 +3 = 3500+150 is 3650, plus 70 is 3720, plus 3 is 3723. Yep, same result. \n\nSo all methods confirm that the product is 3723. I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 51 and 73?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 73 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens places.\n1. Multiply 51 by the ones place digit (3):  \n   \\(51 \\times 3 = 153\\).\n2. Multiply 51 by the tens place digit (70):  \n   \\(51 \\times 70 = 3570\\).  \n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(153 + 3570 = 3723\\).  \n\nSo, the final computed product is **3723**.",
