carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place: 1 (from 153) + 5 (from 3570) plus the carried 1 = 7.\n\nThousands place: 3 (from 3570) remains.\n\nSo that would be 3723. Okay, so that's correct. \n\nWait, but let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   51\nx73\n------\nFirst multiply 51 by 3: 153\n\nThen multiply 51 by 70 (so shift one position to the left):\n\n51 x 70 = 3570\n\nAdding them together: 153 + 3570 = 3723. Yep, that matches. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (50 + 1)(70 + 3) = 50*70 + 50*3 + 1*70 + 1*3 = 3500 + 150 + 70 +3 = 3500+150 is 3650, plus 70 is 3720, plus 3 is 3723. Yep, same result. \n\nSo all methods confirm that the product is 3723. I think that's the correct answer.\n"]
