istributive property. 62 *24 can be written as 62*(20 +4) = 62*20 +62*4, which is exactly what I did. So that gives me confidence. Alternatively, maybe do 60*24 + 2*24. Let's see: 60*24 is 1440, and 2*24 is 48. Adding those gives 1440 +48=1488. Yep, same result. Okay, that checks out. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the standard vertical multiplication:\n\n   62\nx 24\n-------\nFirst multiply 62 by 4: 248\nThen multiply 62 by 20 (so shift one position to the left):\n   62\nx 20\n-----\n1240\n\nAdding 248 and 1240 gives 1488. All methods are leading me to the same answer. I think that's correct. \n\nI don't see any mistakes in my calculations. So the product of 62 and 24 is 1488.\n"]
