te it out vertically:\n\n\u2003\xa014\n×73\n-------\nFirst, multiply 14 by 3 (the ones place): 14×3=42. Write down 42.\nThen multiply 14 by 70 (the tens place). So 14×7=98, then add a zero to get 980.\nAdd 42 and 980: 42+980=1022. Okay, that matches. But wait, let me check with another method just to be sure.\n\nAnother way is to use distributive property: (10 + 4)(70 + 3). Expanding this, it's 10×70 + 10×3 + 4×70 + 4×3. Let's calculate each term:\n\n10×70 = 700,\n\n10×3 = 30,\n\n4×70 = 280,\n\n4×3 = 12.\n\nAdding all those together: 700 + 30 is 730, plus 280 is 1010, plus 12 is 1022. Okay, so that also gives the same result. Hmm, so maybe I was right the first time. Wait, but I initially thought maybe I made a mistake. Let me try another check.\n\nAlternatively, 14 times 70 is 980, plus 14 times 3 is 42, so 980 +42 is indeed 1022. Alright, so that seems consistent. I think that's the correct answer then. Maybe I was just second-guessing myself unnecessarily. So the final product should be 1022.\n"]
