he standard multiplication algorithm. \n\nMultiplying 45 by 7 gives 315. Then multiplying 45 by 80 (since the 8 is in the tens place, so shifted one position to the left). 45 times 8 is 360, so 360 with a zero at the end makes 3600. Adding 315 and 3600 gives 3915. Yep, same result. Okay, that seems right. I think that's the correct answer.\n"]
