er method to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n     97\nx   71\n--------\nFirst multiply 97 by 1: 97\nThen multiply 97 by 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place): 6790\nAdding those gives 97 + 6790 = 6887. \n\nAlternatively, I can use the distributive property: (90 +7)(70 +1) but that might complicate. Alternatively, maybe I can compute 97*71 as (100 -3)(70 +1) but that might not be necessary. Let me see:\n\nAlternatively, 97 *71. Let me try another way. Let me do 97*70 first, which is 6790, then add 97*1 =97, totaling 6887. Same result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe check with calculator math. Wait, since I can't use a calculator, but let me do 71*100 =7100, subtract 71*3 =213, so 7100 -213 = 6887. Yes, that works. \n\nSo all methods lead to 6887. Therefore, the product is 6887. \n\nWait, just to make sure, perhaps I made an addition mistake earlier. Let's confirm the addition again:\n\n6790 + 97. \n\n6790 + 97. Let's add 6790 + 100 = 6890, then subtract 3 (since 97 is 100-3), so 6890 -3 = 6887. Yes, that's correct. \n\nAlright, so the steps are correct. The answer is 6887.\n"] 73%|███████▎  | 367/500 [3:23:53<1:17:01, 34.75s/it] 74%|███████▎  | 368/500 [3:24:16<1:08:58, 31.35s/it]
