em. 86 plus 3010. 3010 + 80 is 3090, then +6 is 3096. So the total should be 3096?\n\nWait, but let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe using the distributive property: (40 +3)(70 +2) = 40\u00d770 +40\u00d72 +3\u00d770 +3\u00d72. \n\nCalculating each term:\n\n40\u00d770 = 2800\n\n40\u00d72 = 80\n\n3\u00d770 = 210\n\n3\u00d72 =6\n\nAdding all together: 2800 +80 = 2880; 2880 +210 = 3090; 3090 +6= 3096. Okay, same result. So that seems right.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do 43\u00d772 as 43\u00d7(70+2) which is the same as above. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using another approach: 72\u00d743. Let me see if I get the same answer. 72\u00d740 = 2880, and 72\u00d73=216. Adding those gives 2880 +216 = 3096. Yep, same answer. \n\nSo the product should be 3096. I think that's correct. Let me just check with a calculator in my mind. 43 times 70 is 3010, plus 43 times 2 is 86. 3010 +86 is 3096. Yep, that's consistent. Okay, so I think that's the right answer.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 43 and 72?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 72 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens place.\n1. Multiply 43 by the ones place digit (2):  \n   \\(43 \\times 2 = 86\\).  \n2. Multiply 43 by the tens place digit (70):  \n   \\(43 \\times 70 = 3010\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(86 + 3010 = 3096\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **3096**.",
