, maybe use the standard algorithm:\n\n   96\nx 38\n-----\nFirst step: 96 x 8 = 768\nSecond step: 96 x 30 = 2880 (written as 2880 shifted one left)\nAdding those gives 3648. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use another method like distributive property: (90 + 6)(30 + 8) = 90*30 + 90*8 + 6*30 + 6*8. Let's compute each term:\n\n90*30 = 2700\n\n90*8 = 720\n\n6*30 = 180\n\n6*8 = 48\n\nAdding all these: 2700 + 720 is 3420, plus 180 is 3600, plus 48 is 3648. Yep, same result. \n\nSo seems like 3648 is the correct answer. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in the calculations here. All methods lead to the same result, so I feel confident.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 96 and 38?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 38 has two digits, so we'll break it into ones and tens:  \n1. Multiply 96 by the ones place digit (8):  \n   \\( 96 \\times 8 = 768 \\).  \n2. Multiply 96 by the tens place digit (30):  \n   \\( 96 \\times 30 = 2,\\!880 \\).  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 768 + 2,\\!880 = 3,\\!648 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **3,648**.",
