soning had three steps because the second number was three digits. Here, since 36 is two digits, there should be two steps. The user's example for 153 had steps 1 and 2, so here step 1 is 26*6, step 2 is 26*30, and then sum them. The other digits part can be omitted since there are only two digits. \n\nSo the reasoning should be written as:\n\n1. Multiply 26 by the ones place digit 6 of 36: 26 \u00d7 6 = 156.\n2. Multiply 26 by the tens place digit 30 of 36: 26 \u00d7 30 = 780.\n\nThen the answer part would sum 156 + 780 = 936. \n\nI need to make sure the numbers are written correctly and the steps are clear. Also, in the answer section, the user's template has \"sum of the results\" and \"final computed product\". So putting it all together in the required format.\n</think>\n\n",
