t's try the standard algorithm:\n\n   49\nx 65\n-------\nFirst multiply 49 by 5: 245\n\nThen multiply 49 by 60 (so shifted one position to the left):\n\n49 x60 = 2940\n\nAdding them gives 245 +2940 = 3185. Yep, same result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using distributive property: 49*(60+5)=49*60 +49*5=2940+245=3185. \n\nAlternatively, maybe break down 65 into 60+5 and compute both parts. That's exactly what I did. \n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 50*65 + 0*65? Wait, no. Wait, 49 is 50-1. So maybe (50 -1)*65 = 50*65 -1*65. Let's see:\n\n50*65 = 3250, and 1*65=65. So 3250-65=3185. That also gives the same answer. So that confirms it again. \n\nSo I think the answer is 3185. I don't see any mistakes in my steps, so I'm confident that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
