(since the 7 is in the tens place). 33 × 70 is indeed 2310. Adding them gives 297 + 2310 = 2607. \n\nHmm, that matches my previous result. Let me confirm with another approach. Maybe using the distributive property in a different way. \n\n33 × 79 can be thought of as (30 + 3) × (70 + 9). Expanding that:\n\n30×70 + 30×9 + 3×70 + 3×9\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n30×70 = 2100\n\n30×9 = 270\n\n3×70 = 210\n\n3×9 = 27\n\nNow add them all together: 2100 + 270 is 2370. Then 2370 + 210 is 2580. Then 2580 +27 is 2607. Yep, same answer again. \n\nSo all methods lead me to 2607. I think that's the correct product. Let me just check once more with a calculator approach. \n\n33 multiplied by 79. Let's see: 30*80 is 2400, but since it's 79, that's one less. So 30*(80-1) = 30*79 = 2370. Then add 3*79. Wait, no, that's not the way. Wait, actually, 33 is 30 +3, so 33*79 = 30*79 + 3*79. \n\n30*79: 30*70=2100, 30*9=270, so total 2370. \n\n3*79 is 237. \n\nAdding 2370 +237: 2370 +200 is 2570, plus 37 is 2607. \n\nYep, same result. Okay, I'm confident now. The answer should be 2607.\n"]
