o, let me write it vertically:\n\n  2170\n+  279\n--------\nStarting from the ones digit:\n0 +9 =9\n7 (tens place) +7 (from 279's tens) =14, so write 4, carryover 1.\n1 (hundreds place of 2170) +2 (hundreds from 279) +1 (carryover) =4\n2 (thousands place) remains as is, so 2.\n\nThus, total is 2449. Okay, that's consistent.\n\nWait, but just to confirm, maybe I should do the multiplication another way to cross-verify. Let's try the standard algorithm for 31\u00d779.\n\n31\n\u00d779\n------\nFirst multiply 31 by 9: 279 (as before)\nThen multiply 31 by 70: 2170 (as before)\nAdd them: 279+2170=2449. So same result. That's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property another way: (30+1)(70+9) = 30\u00d770 +30\u00d79 +1\u00d770 +1\u00d79. Let's compute each term:\n\n30\u00d770 = 2100,\n\n30\u00d79 =270,\n\n1\u00d770=70,\n\n1\u00d79=9.\n\nAdding all together: 2100 +270 is 2370, plus 70 is 2440, plus 9 is 2449. Yep, same answer. So that confirms it again.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 31\u00d780 minus 31, since 79 is 80-1. Let's see: 31\u00d780=2480, then subtract 31 gives 2480-31=2449. Yep, that works too. So all methods lead to the same answer, so I'm confident that 31\u00d779=2449.\n\nTherefore, following the template, the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 31 by 9 (the ones place of 79) to get 279.\n\n2. Multiply 31 by 70 (the tens place of 79) to get 2170.\n\nSum those two: 279 + 2170 = 2449. So the final answer is 2449.\n</think>\n\n",
