, but 31 times 39... Let me verify with another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n   31\nx39\n------\nFirst multiply 31 by 9: 279. Then multiply 31 by 30 (since the 3 is in the tens place), which is 930. Then add them: 279 + 930 = 1209. Yep, that's the same result. \n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property: (30 +1)(30 +9) but that might complicate. Let me see: 30*30 + 30*9 +1*30 +1*9 = 900 +270 +30 +9 = 900+270 is 1170, plus 30 is 1200, plus 9 is 1209. So same answer. \n\nHmm, so I think that's correct. So the final answer should be 1209. Let me just make sure I didn't make any arithmetic errors. \n\nAnother way: 31 times 40 would be 1240, right? Because 31*40 is 31*4*10 = 124*10=1240. But since it's 39, that's one less 31. So 1240 -31 = 1209. Yep, that works. \n\nOkay, so all methods lead to 1209. I think that's solid.\n</think>\n\n",
