u00d789 = 67\u00d7(90 -1) = 67\u00d790 - 67\u00d71. \n\nCalculating 67\u00d790: 67\u00d79=603, so times 10 is 6030. Then subtract 67: 6030 - 67 = 5963. Yep, same result. Okay, so that confirms it. \n\nTherefore, the product of 67 and 89 is indeed 5963.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 67 and 89?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 89 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens places.\n1. Multiply 67 by the ones place digit 9:  \n   \\(67 \\times 9 = 603\\).  \n2. Multiply 67 by the tens place digit 80:  \n   \\(67 \\times 80 = 5,\\!360\\).  \nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(603 + 5,\\!360 = 5,\\!963\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **5,963**.",
