by 89:\n\nFirst, write it down:\n\n\u2003\xa067\n×89\n------\nFirst multiply 67 by 9 (the ones place): 67×9=603\nThen multiply 67 by 80 (the tens place): 67×80=5360\nAdding them together: 603 + 5360 = 5963. \n\nHmm, that matches. But just to be absolutely sure, maybe do the multiplication another way. Let's see, perhaps using the distributive property: (70 - 3)(90 - 1). Wait, maybe that complicates things. Alternatively, 67×89 = 67×(90 -1) = 67×90 - 67×1. \n\nCalculating 67×90: 67×9=603, so times 10 is 6030. Then subtract 67: 6030 - 67 = 5963. Yep, same result. Okay, so that confirms it. \n\nTherefore, the product of 67 and 89 is indeed 5963.\n"] 84%|████████▍ | 422/500 [3:53:42<41:59, 32.30s/it] 85%|████████▍ | 423/500 [3:54:28<46:53, 36.54s/it]
