hen I did the other way, I thought of 3050 + 183 as 3050 + 100 = 3150, plus 80 is 3230, plus 3 is 3233. Okay, so that's correct. Wait, but earlier when I thought of 3000 + 100, etc., I messed up the breakdown. So the correct total is 3233?\n\nWait, but let me verify using another method. Maybe the standard multiplication algorithm to check.\n\nMultiplying 61 by 53:\n\nFirst, write 61\n×53\n-----\nMultiply 61 by 3: 183\nMultiply 61 by 50 (shift one position to the left): 3050\nAdd them: 183 + 3050 = 3233. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, so why did I get confused earlier? Maybe I miscalculated when I broke it into 3000 + 100 etc. But the step-by-step addition shows it's 3233. Okay, so that must be the right answer. Let me just confirm with another method, like the lattice method or another approach.\n\nAlternatively, 61 × 53 can be thought of as (60 +1)(50 +3) = 60×50 + 60×3 +1×50 +1×3 = 3000 + 180 +50 +3 = 3000+180 is 3180, plus 50 is 3230, plus 3 is 3233. Yep, same result. Okay, so that's solid. So the product is 3233.\n"]
