ss 13. So 650 -13 = 637. That works too. \n\nAll methods lead to 637, so I think that's the correct answer. I don't see any mistakes in my steps. Let me just confirm once more with direct multiplication:\n\n13 multiplied by 49. \n\n49 times 10 is 490, and 49 times 3 is 147. Adding 490 + 147 gives 637. Yep, that checks out. Alright, confident now that the answer is 637.\n"]
