 5236. Let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n     68\nx   77\n-------\nFirst multiply 68 by 7 (ones place): 68*7=476\nThen multiply 68 by 70 (the tens place, so shift one position): 68*70=4760\nAdd them together: 476 + 4760 = 5236. Yep, same result. Okay, that seems right.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 68 and 77?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 77 has two digits, so we can break it into ones and tens places.\n1. Multiply 68 by the ones place digit 7:  \n   \\(68 \\times 7 = 476\\).  \n2. Multiply 68 by the tens place digit (70):  \n   \\(68 \\times 70 = 4760\\).  \nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(476 + 4760 = 5236\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{5236}.",
