ertically:\n\n   4760\n+   476\n--------\nStarting from the right:\n0 + 6 = 6\n6 + 7 = 13, carry over 1\n7 (hundreds place) + 4 (hundreds) plus the carried 1 = 12, so write 2 and carry 1\n4 (thousands) + 0 (since 476 has no thousands beyond the first digit) plus the carried 1 = 5\n\nSo the total is 5236. Wait, but when I first added 4760 + 476, 4760 + 400 is 5160, plus 76 is 5236. Yeah, that's correct.\n\nSo the total product should be 5236. Let me verify using another method to be sure. Maybe the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n     68\nx   77\n-------\nFirst multiply 68 by 7 (ones place): 68*7=476\nThen multiply 68 by 70 (the tens place, so shift one position): 68*70=4760\nAdd them together: 476 + 4760 = 5236. Yep, same result. Okay, that seems right.\n"] 87%|████████▋ | 434/500 [4:00:32<38:44, 35.22s/it] 87%|████████▋ | 435/500 [4:01:01<36:16, 33.49s/it]
