ply 85 by the ones digit (5) to get 425. Second step: multiply 85 by the tens digit (8), but since it's the tens place, it's actually 80, so 85*80=6800. Then adding those two gives 7225. Yep, that's correct. \n\nI think that's all. The final answer should be 7225. Let me confirm with another method. Maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n   85\nx 85\n-----\n  425  (85 x 5)\n+6800 (85 x 80)\n-----\n 7225\n\nYes, that's the same. Okay, confident now.\n</think>\n\n",
