e carried over 1=7. Wait, maybe I should do it step by step.\n\nWait, 444\n\n+6660\n\n--------\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes place: 4 +0 =4\n\nTens place: 4 +6 =10, write down 0 and carry over 1.\n\nHundreds place: 4 +6 =10, plus the carried 1 makes 11. Write down 1, carry over 1.\n\nThousands place: 6 (from 6660) plus the carried 1 =7.\n\nSo the total is 7104?\n\nWait, wait. Wait 444 + 6660:\n\nLet me do it another way. 6660 + 400 is 7060, then +44 is 7104. Yes, that's correct. So the total is 7104.\n\nWait but let me double-check the multiplication steps again to be sure I didn't make an error there. \n\nFirst step: 74 ×6. 70×6 is 420, 4×6 is 24. 420+24 is indeed 444. That's right.\n\nSecond step: 74 ×90. Let's see, 74×9 is 666. Then times 10 is 6660. Correct. \n\nAdding 444 and 6660 gives 7104. So that should be the answer.\n\nAlternatively, just to confirm, maybe I can compute 74×96 directly using another method. Let's see:\n\n74×96. Maybe using the standard algorithm:\n\n   74\n\n×96\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 74 by 6: 444\n\nThen multiply 74 by 90 (which is 74×9 shifted one position to the left, then ×10). So 74×9 is 666, so 6660. Then add 444 +6660 =7104. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, use distributive property: 74×(100 -4) =74×100 -74×4 =7400 -296 = 7400-296. Let's compute that: 7400 - 200 is 7200, then subtract 96 more: 7200 -96 = 7104. Yep, same answer. So that confirms it. \n\nTherefore, the product of 74 and 96 is 7104. I think that's solid. The steps in the reasoning should reflect breaking down the multiplication into the ones and tens places, multiplying each part, then adding. So the answer is 7104.\n"] 88%|████████▊ | 441/500 [4:04:25<37:17, 37.93s/it] 88%|████████▊ | 442/500 [4:04:56<34:29, 35.67s/it]
