y 92 by 7: 644 (as before). \n\nThen multiply 92 by 50. Since the 5 is in the tens place, we shift one position to the left. So 92×5 is 460, then add a zero to make it 4600. \n\nAdding 644 and 4600 gives 5244. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (90 + 2)(50 +7) = 90*50 + 90*7 + 2*50 + 2*7. Let's see:\n\n90*50 = 4500  \n90*7 = 630  \n2*50 = 100  \n2*7 =14  \n\nAdding those together: 4500 + 630 = 5130; 5130 +100 = 5230; 5230 +14 = 5244. Yep, same result. \n\nOkay, so that seems to check out. I think the answer is 5244. Let me just confirm with a calculator in my head another way. 57 times 90 is 5130, and 57 times 2 is 114. Adding those gives 5130 + 114 = 5244. Yep, that works. \n\nAlright, I'm confident now that the product of 92 and 57 is indeed 5244.\n"]
