d step: 41\u00d760=2460\n\nAdding them gives 41 +2460 =2501. So that's correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do straight multiplication:\n\n   41\n\u00d7 61\n-------\n   41  (41\u00d71)\n+2460 (41\u00d760, shifted one position to the left)\n-------\n  2501\n\nYes, that's right. So the final answer should be 2501. I think that's correct. Let me just do a quick check using another approach. Maybe approximate? 40\u00d760 is 2400, and 41\u00d761 is a bit more, which 2501 is reasonable. Alternatively, 41\u00d760 is 2460, plus another 41 gives 2501. Yep, that's correct.\n</think>\n\n",
