n multiply 49 by 70 (since the 7 is in the tens place, so shifted one position to the left):\n   49\nx70\n-----\n3430 (same as before)\nAdding those two gives 441 + 3430 = 3871. Yep, that matches. So I think that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 49 and 79?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 79 has two digits, so we can reason in two steps.\n1. Multiply 49 by the ones place digit 9 of 79:  \n   \\(49 \\times 9 = 441\\).  \n2. Multiply 49 by the tens place digit 70 of 79:  \n   \\(49 \\times 70 = 3430\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(441 + 3430 = 3871\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **3871**.",
