e two results (0 + 1840) which is 1840. Yep, same answer.\n\nHmm, so all methods are pointing to 1840. I think that's the correct product. Let me just confirm once more with another approach. \n\nBreaking down 80 into 100 - 20, but that might complicate. Alternatively, 23 is 20 +3, so 80*(20+3)=80*20 +80*3=1600+240=1840. Yep, same as before. Okay, I'm confident now that the answer is 1840.\n</think>\n\n",
