ee:\n\n50\u00d730=1500\n\n50\u00d76=300\n\n8\u00d730=240\n\n8\u00d76=48\n\nAdding all those: 1500 +300 is 1800, plus 240 is 2040, plus 48 is 2088. Yep, same answer again. \n\nOkay, so all methods lead to 2088. I think that's the correct product. I don't see any mistakes in my steps, so I'm confident the answer is right.\n</think>\n\n",
