Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 43 has two digits, so we can break it into two steps:\n1. Multiply 87 by the ones place digit (3):  \n   \\(87 \\times 3 = 261\\).  \n2. Multiply 87 by the tens place digit (40):  \n   \\(87 \\times 40 = 3,\\!480\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(261 + 3,\\!480 = 3,\\!741\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{3741}.",
