 the right:\n0 + 2 = 2\n6 + 5 = 11, write down 1, carry over 1\n9 + 2 = 11, plus the carried 1 makes 12, write down 2, carry over 1\n1 + 0 (since 252 has no thousands) plus the carried 1 is 2.\n\nSo that gives 2212. Hmm, but I thought maybe there's a mistake here. Let me cross-verify using another multiplication method. Maybe the standard algorithm?\n\nMultiplying 28 by 79:\n\nFirst, write 28  \n×79  \n________\n\nMultiply 28 by 9 (the ones place): 28×9=252. Write that down.  \nThen multiply 28 by 70 (the tens place, so shift one position to the left): 28×70=1960.  \nAdding those two: 252 + 1960 = 2212. That's the same result as before. \n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property: (20 + 8) × (70 + 9) = 20×70 + 20×9 + 8×70 + 8×9. Let's compute each term:\n\n20×70 = 1400  \n20×9 = 180  \n8×70 = 560  \n8×9 = 72  \nAdding all together: 1400 + 180 = 1580; 1580 + 560 = 2140; 2140 + 72 = 2212. \n\nSame answer again. Okay, so maybe I was just second-guessing unnecessarily. The answer is 2212. \n\nWait, but let me check with a calculator method. 28 × 79. Let me compute 28×80 which is 2240, then subtract 28 to get 2240 - 28 = 2212. Yes, that works too. So all methods confirm that it's 2212. Therefore, the final answer is correct.\n"] 98%|█████████▊| 489/500 [4:31:46<06:05, 33.27s/it] 98%|█████████▊| 490/500 [4:32:12<05:11, 31.16s/it]
